Two-bin p_pi scheme, adopted 2026-08-17.

The range-based pion momentum saturates near 0.34 GeV/c (pions interact hadronically
before stopping), so the five-bin scheme had migration diagonals 99/24/13/6/6 against
the >68% usable-bin criterion used by the BNB CC1pi analysis -- only the first bin
qualified. Merging everything above the first bin recovers what can honestly be
resolved: 97.4% / 61.9%.

Boundary 0.205 GeV/c is the optimum. The worst diagonal is always bin 2 and it falls
monotonically as the boundary rises, so the binding constraint is bin-1 WIDTH, not the
diagonal; 30 MeV/c matches the narrowest bin in the BNB analysis. Measured trade-off
(held-out run):
    0.185 (10 MeV)  95.8 / 69.3
    0.200 (25 MeV)  97.1 / 63.8
    0.205 (30 MeV)  97.4 / 61.9   <- adopted
    0.250 (75 MeV)  99.2 / 46.4

A three-bin variant was tested and is WORSE: the best possible is 97/38/39, because
above ~0.25 GeV/c the estimator barely varies, so a second boundary up there separates
almost nothing. Adding the third bin costs ~25 points on the worst bin.
